WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.267
-Welcome back.
-Jimmy!

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:03.400
-Hi.
-Look at you.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.200
The hardest-working people
in show business.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.267
-Oh, stop it. You are.

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:07.801
-You start the network
in the morning

00:00:07.801 --> 00:00:08.801
and you're closing --

00:00:08.801 --> 00:00:10.033
-We're shutting it down!

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:11.334
-Shutting it down with
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:12.968
Come on.
-Come on.

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:14.300
-Thank you again
for coming back.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.667
I always love seeing you.
I watch you every single day.

00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:18.767
You finally got a little
time off during the holidays.

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:19.834
-We did.
-A little break.

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:21.167
-Oh, my God.
-What'd you do?

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:23.667
-Okay, so, Jimmy,
I took my two girls,

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:25.067
Haley and Hope, to Universal.

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:26.334
-They're the cutest kids.

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:28.834
-First of all, they met you,
and they adore you,

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:31.534
so when we were
walking around, I go,

00:00:31.534 --> 00:00:33.167
"Look -- there's
a Jimmy Fallon ride!"

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:34.567
-I have my own ride.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:38.567
-Wait. You have your own --
Have y'all ever been on it?

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:40.701
It's -- Okay, it's really fun.

00:00:40.701 --> 00:00:42.334
So, my 3-year-old
put the glasses on.

00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:44.133
You get locked in.

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:45.834
It's like you're in
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:49.601
Jimmy, she was terrified.

00:00:49.601 --> 00:00:51.167
She is, like, scarred.

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:52.367
-I don't think she can do that.

00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:54.868
-She loved you, but now --
-She's too young.

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:56.100
-Yeah, she just --
-Did she throw up?

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.234
-She just made the height.
She didn't throw up.

00:00:57.234 --> 00:00:58.467
-Did she understand
what was happening?

00:00:58.467 --> 00:00:59.834
-Jimmy, she was terrified.

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:01.968
She kept going, "Where's Jimmy?
Where's Jimmy? No!

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:03.767
Get me out, get me out,
get me out!"

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:05.501
And you can't get out
once you're in.

00:01:05.501 --> 00:01:07.767
-Just like "The Tonight Show."
Yeah, they're all strapped in.

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.200
They're not allowed to leave.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.567
-By the way, it was super-fun,
but she was way too little.

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:13.601
But you have to, like,
come and hug her.

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:15.200
-Alright, next time,
bring her over.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.601
Yeah, yeah,
I'll come by and see you.

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:18.400
How about -- You have
a birthday around Christmas.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:19.634
-Yes, I do.

00:01:19.634 --> 00:01:21.534
The coveted
two-days-after-Christmas

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:25.067
birthday, when everybody was
really in the mood to celebrate.

00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:27.334
And, also, I turned 51,
which is so not exciting.

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:30.067
-Oh, my gosh. Happy birthday!
Yes! Come on.

00:01:30.067 --> 00:01:32.501
-Yes, it is exciting.

00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:34.734
-But my little boy asked me,
literally, the other day --

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:36.100
You know how,
when they're little,

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.033
they have the 4-year-old visit,
the 5-year-old visit?

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:39.567
My little boy goes, "Mommy,

00:01:39.567 --> 00:01:41.300
did you have your
51-year-old visit?"

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.634
-Oh, no.
-I know.

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:44.801
And I was like, "Yeah,
they weighed and measured me.

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:46.367
I got the shingles vaccine."

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:48.901
Yeah, so, we did that,
and it was fun.

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:50.100
-It was fun?
A little family time?

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.534
Did you get any good gifts?

00:01:51.534 --> 00:01:52.834
-You know what
the cutest thing is?

00:01:52.834 --> 00:01:55.734
The kids actually wrote down
what they liked about me,

00:01:55.734 --> 00:01:56.734
which is really --

00:01:56.734 --> 00:01:58.167
-Are you joking?
-I know.

00:01:58.167 --> 00:02:00.701
And I think they were, like,
you know, prompted to do that.

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:02.000
-Yeah.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.234
-But my little boy said
I smelled good.

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:05.567
-Hey!
-Yes.

00:02:05.567 --> 00:02:09.634
And my daughter said,
"She acts like a little girl"

00:02:09.634 --> 00:02:11.567
and that I sing, but badly.

00:02:11.567 --> 00:02:12.767
-No!
-Yes.

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:14.334
-Still, you take it.
That's so cute.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:15.901
-Yeah.
-Come on.

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:17.667
Before we talk about
the five years,

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:19.601
I want to talk about your
new podcast.

00:02:19.601 --> 00:02:20.734
Talk to me about this.
"Making Space."

00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:23.234
-By the way,
I love this podcast, Jimmy.

00:02:23.234 --> 00:02:24.868
There are certain things you do
and you're crazy about.

00:02:24.868 --> 00:02:27.567
This whole --
This podcast is all kind of

00:02:27.567 --> 00:02:30.367
inspirational leaders
and teachers.

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:31.801
-You love -- You're good at --
You love that.

00:02:31.801 --> 00:02:33.334
-I'm so -- I'm so in.

00:02:33.334 --> 00:02:35.501
I feel like if I wasn't doing
the podcast, like,

00:02:35.501 --> 00:02:37.000
I would be listening to it.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.033
But we had this lady on
named Mel Robbins,

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.467
who's a very, like --
she's a motivational speaker.

00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:41.567
-Yeah.

00:02:41.567 --> 00:02:43.100
-And she was saying to --
She was saying,

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:45.534
"Look, in the new year,
you should do --

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:47.334
You can start off by
this resolution."

00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:48.868
She said,
"The very first decision

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:50.400
you make every morning
when you wake up,

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.567
the very, very first decision
when your alarm goes off is,

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:55.200
you're going to decide whether
or not you're going to

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.334
procrastinate to start your day
or you're going to hop up."

00:02:58.334 --> 00:03:00.100
She said, "The very first
decision you make

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.267
in the morning,
never ever hit snooze.

00:03:02.267 --> 00:03:06.234
Feet on the floor, get up,
get into the shower right away.

00:03:06.234 --> 00:03:08.534
Make your bed right away."

00:03:08.534 --> 00:03:10.300
And she said,
"Once you do those things --"

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:11.601
-I don't know.
I don't know about this.

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:12.968
-Jimmy, that means the whole --

00:03:12.968 --> 00:03:15.834
-I might do the first one,
but I can't do both things.

00:03:15.834 --> 00:03:16.968
-That's too much?

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:18.267
-Feels like I'm in the...
-It's a lot?

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:19.434
-...yeah, the armed forces.

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:22.567
I want to talk about
"Today," okay?

00:03:22.567 --> 00:03:26.968
This is
a landmark show, obviously,

00:03:26.968 --> 00:03:29.334
one of the --
"Tonight Show," "Today Show."

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:33.567
Recently, we lost a legend,
journalist Barbara Walters,

00:03:33.567 --> 00:03:35.868
who was on the "Today" show
for 15 years?

00:03:35.868 --> 00:03:36.968
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:36.968 --> 00:03:38.367
-What did her legacy
leave behind?

00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:40.200
What does she mean to you guys?

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.334
-Well, she -- I think she said
it best when we --

00:03:42.334 --> 00:03:44.033
A few years ago, when she
retired from "The View,"

00:03:44.033 --> 00:03:46.734
they invited newswomen
past and present,

00:03:46.734 --> 00:03:48.467
and everyone walked out
and surprised her.

00:03:48.467 --> 00:03:49.767
And, I mean,
everybody was there.

00:03:49.767 --> 00:03:51.467
Oprah was there, everyone.

00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:52.567
And Barbara looked around,

00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:55.000
and she said,
"You guys are my legacy."

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.968
And I think we know
that that is true.

00:03:56.968 --> 00:03:59.133
I mean, at the "Today" show
in particular,

00:03:59.133 --> 00:04:01.200
we're not here without
Barbara Walters

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.334
knocking down that door
and doing it when

00:04:03.334 --> 00:04:04.467
there was no precedent.

00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:05.634
There was no example.

00:04:05.634 --> 00:04:08.634
There was no representation
of that path.

00:04:08.634 --> 00:04:09.767
She did it.

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:11.868
She blazed the trail
like a pioneer.

00:04:11.868 --> 00:04:14.300
-We are able to sit and have
two women anchoring together,

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:18.234
which is now totally normal,
because of what Barbara did.

00:04:18.234 --> 00:04:19.834
-Yeah, you say Barbara --
Yeah, of course.

00:04:19.834 --> 00:04:21.901
She was a trailblazer.
But think about that.

00:04:21.901 --> 00:04:23.868
That's five years
of doing this together.

00:04:23.868 --> 00:04:27.367
When you first were sat together
and you opened the "Today" show,

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:29.100
did it feel like
a moment to you?

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.467
-It felt like a moment, but not
because it was two women.

00:04:31.467 --> 00:04:32.868
It was because it was us.
-Yeah.

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:35.934
-You know, it was --
We literally held hands

00:04:35.934 --> 00:04:37.167
and said, "Let's do this."

00:04:37.167 --> 00:04:38.334
-"Let's go."
-You know?

00:04:38.334 --> 00:04:40.267
-But it was a moment
for women, I would think.

00:04:40.267 --> 00:04:41.434
-I think it was.

00:04:41.434 --> 00:04:42.834
We didn't realize it,
because I remember,

00:04:42.834 --> 00:04:44.534
I went to
a SoulCycle spin class

00:04:44.534 --> 00:04:47.200
and I walked in shortly after
Savannah and I had started.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.167
And I sat in the same seat
I always sit in,

00:04:49.167 --> 00:04:50.868
in Sue's SoulCycle class.

00:04:50.868 --> 00:04:52.801
And I sat in my chair,
and people started clapping.

00:04:52.801 --> 00:04:54.567
And I was like, "Oh, my God.
Someone has a birthday."

00:04:54.567 --> 00:04:56.567
You know, they always do --
You know how they do.

00:04:56.567 --> 00:04:58.300
-Yeah, yeah, the bike clap.
They root for each other.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:00.067
They're like, "You go!"
-"You got it! Yeah!"

00:05:00.067 --> 00:05:02.601
-"You got it."
-"50 looks good!" Anyway...

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:04.567
And as I was sitting,
I was looking around,

00:05:04.567 --> 00:05:05.634
and they were looking at me.

00:05:05.634 --> 00:05:07.834
And I said --
I go, "What's going on?"

00:05:07.834 --> 00:05:10.701
And they go, "What you and
Savannah did today.

00:05:10.701 --> 00:05:12.400
It was big. It was big."

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:14.801
And I told Savannah --
I said, "Oh, my God.

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:15.968
It mattered."

00:05:15.968 --> 00:05:17.868
Like, we didn't realize,
I think, in the moment

00:05:17.868 --> 00:05:19.167
that it did, and now --

00:05:19.167 --> 00:05:21.968
-Have you seen things
change since you've started?

00:05:21.968 --> 00:05:23.667
-You know one thing
that we notice a lot?

00:05:23.667 --> 00:05:26.234
Is in local news,
which we came up in local news,

00:05:26.234 --> 00:05:29.133
you know, if somebody
was gone and you needed a sub,

00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:30.634
it was always a guy and a girl.

00:05:30.634 --> 00:05:31.868
It was always a man and a woman.

00:05:31.868 --> 00:05:33.901
It was like Dina and Todd
or whoever and whoever.

00:05:33.901 --> 00:05:35.300
They would never
put two women --

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.534
They would never say,
"Oh, Todd's off tonight.

00:05:37.534 --> 00:05:38.901
Hoda, can you fill in? Savannah?

00:05:38.901 --> 00:05:40.767
No, we can't have two women."
-Two women.

00:05:40.767 --> 00:05:43.100
-Now we notice, because we do
all these affiliate cross-tags,

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:44.734
so we see it
in local news all the time.

00:05:44.734 --> 00:05:46.834
There are a lot of
female partnerships.

00:05:46.834 --> 00:05:50.234
So, I don't know if that's --
Probably not because of us,

00:05:50.234 --> 00:05:51.901
but now it's just more normal.

00:05:51.901 --> 00:05:53.334
And I think that's really cool.

00:05:53.334 --> 00:05:55.100
-I think it is
because of you guys, yeah.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:56.501
-Todd shouldn't have taken
all that time off.

00:05:56.501 --> 00:05:57.634
-No, exactly right, yeah.

00:05:57.634 --> 00:05:58.701
-And you know what else
is really cool?

00:05:58.701 --> 00:06:00.067
-Yeah.

00:06:00.067 --> 00:06:02.367
-Guess who's coming back
tomorrow, Jimmy, on our show.

00:06:02.367 --> 00:06:03.467
-Al.
-Guess who's coming back.

00:06:03.467 --> 00:06:04.501
-Al Roker?
-Yes!

00:06:04.501 --> 00:06:06.400
-Al Roker's back?
-Yes.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:07.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
-We love you, Al.

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:09.901
No, no, no.
I'm going to lose it.

00:06:09.901 --> 00:06:12.000
I love -- I'm going to lose it.
I love that guy so much.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.167
-You sent him such cool videos
when he was in the hospital.

00:06:13.167 --> 00:06:15.033
-He's such a good guy.
I can't wait.

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:16.300
Alright, good.

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:18.734
I'll try to watch --
I'll come in tomorrow early

00:06:18.734 --> 00:06:19.968
just to say hi to Al.

00:06:19.968 --> 00:06:21.100
-You'll have to wake up
in the morning hours.

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:22.868
-I won't hit snooze.
Yeah, exactly.

00:06:22.868 --> 00:06:24.501
But, really,
I wanted to thank you for

00:06:24.501 --> 00:06:26.067
coming on the show again,
but also to thank you for what

00:06:26.067 --> 00:06:27.434
you're doing
and what you've done.

00:06:27.434 --> 00:06:29.367
Five years -- this is massive,
what you're doing.

00:06:29.367 --> 00:06:31.067
And you're the best.
I watch you every morning.

00:06:31.067 --> 00:06:32.167
You're the greatest.
Thank you, guys, so much.

00:06:32.167 --> 00:06:33.801
-Jimmy, we love you.
We love you.

00:06:33.801 --> 00:06:37.200
-Savannah Guthrie, Hoda Kotb --
no one better --

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:38.934
right here on
the "Today" show on NBC.

00:06:38.934 --> 00:06:40.634
We'll be right back
with Colin Quinn, everybody.

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:41.634
Stick around.

